    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n46572" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sum-mŏlestus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">subm-</span></b> ), a, um,
			adj., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>somewhat troublesome</i> or <i>vexatious</i> (very rare): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">illud est mihi submolestum, quod, etc.,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Att. 16, 4, 4</span></i>
			.—<i>Adv.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">summŏle-stē</span></b> , <i>with some vexation</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aliquid ferre,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Att. 5, 21, 1</span></i>
			.</div>
